Bundled dependencies in the default, single-node release:

- Zaxonlite 0.7.0 and Paxos 0.7.0: MIT; LICENSES/Zaxonlite-MIT.txt and
  LICENSES/Paxos-MIT.txt. Sources: github.com/insanai/zaxonlite and
  github.com/insanai/paxos-zig. Zig 0.17 compatibility sources are included in vendor/.
  Paxos chosen-history replay preserves ballot-bearing leader evidence and election timers.
  Delayed Nacks cannot replace a newer durable or observed full ballot with an older hint.
  Zaxonlite payloads use named same-directory stages and atomic no-replace installation.
  File, directory and journal durability barriers retain their order. Abandoned stages
  are removed under the node's exclusive data-directory lock during startup.
  Original archives, package hashes, source digests and local corrections are recorded
  in vendor/provenance.json.
  SQLite dependencies remain pinned in vendor/zaxonlite/build.zig.zon.
- SQLite 3.50.4: public domain; sqlite.org/copyright.html. The pinned
  amalgamation is sqlite-amalgamation-3500400.zip.
- sqlite-vec 0.1.9: MIT; LICENSES/sqlite-vec-MIT.txt.
  Source: github.com/asg017/sqlite-vec.
- daisyUI and Tailwind CSS: MIT; LICENSES/daisyUI-MIT.txt and
  LICENSES/Tailwind-MIT.txt. Versions are pinned in
  apps/console-ui/web/package-lock.json. Only generated CSS is bundled;
  Node and npm are not runtime dependencies.
- Natural Earth 5.1.2 geographic geometry: public domain;
  naturalearthdata.com/about/terms-of-use/. Reproduction and source digests
  are in tools/console_geometry.py and the console asset manifest.
- Zig 0.17.0 runtime and standard library: MIT and included notices;
  LICENSES/Zig-LICENSE.txt. Static Linux releases also link musl libc;
  LICENSES/musl-COPYRIGHT.txt.

No GeoIP address database is bundled. Operators import separately licensed
datasets using Sibuna's GeoIP commands. Cluster builds are separate source
builds and link OpenSSL 3; the default release has no OpenSSL dependency.

CRS engine dependencies and compatibility fixtures:

- OWASP Core Rule Set 4.30.0: Apache-2.0; LICENSES/OWASP-CRS-Apache-2.0.txt
  and vendor/crs/LICENSE. Source: github.com/coreruleset/coreruleset.
  Release digest, signing fingerprint and unmodified file digests are in
  vendor/crs/provenance.json. Release packages download and verify the signed
  rules when the operator prepares a candidate; rules are not bundled in the
  executable. Inspection starts when the operator selects Audit or Enforce.
  vendor/crs/fixture.zig is a first-party LGPL-3.0 test facade.
- ModSecurity 3.0.14 compatibility algorithms adapted in
  libs/crs/src/transform_scan.zig, transform_escape.zig, transform_entity.zig
  transform_base64.zig, transform_path.zig and transform_unicode.zig: Apache-2.0;
  LICENSES/ModSecurity-Apache-2.0.txt. Copyright (c) 2015-2023 Trustwave
  Holdings, Inc. Source: github.com/owasp-modsecurity/ModSecurity.
  The native scans use caller-owned buffers and explicit bounds instead of
  the reference's in-place C++ strings. This does not bundle the ModSecurity
  engine or imply complete compatibility. External SecLang test vectors are
  fetched into an ignored cache, not redistributed with Sibuna.
- Mbed TLS commit 2ca6c285a0dd3f33982dd57299012dacab1ff206 base64
  validation semantics adapted in transform_base64.zig:
  Apache-2.0; LICENSES/Mbed-TLS-Apache-2.0.txt. Copyright The Mbed TLS
  Contributors. Source: github.com/Mbed-TLS/mbedtls. The native bounded
  decoder does not link or bundle the Mbed TLS library.
- libinjection dictionary, SQL detection and HTML/XSS algorithms,
  commit b9fcaaf9e50e9492807b23ffcc6af46ee1f203b9:
  BSD-3-Clause; LICENSES/libinjection-BSD-3-Clause.txt and vendor/libinjection/LICENSE.
  Copyright (c) 2012-2016 Nick Galbreath. Source: github.com/libinjection/libinjection.
  The generated native lookup asset and native sql_token_context.zig, sql_tokens*.zig,
  sql_fold*.zig, sql_detector*.zig, html_*.zig and xss_*.zig routines and
  vendor/libinjection/xss_tables.zig
  routines are reproduced or adapted from the pinned source and digests recorded in
  vendor/libinjection/provenance.json. The port uses caller-owned buffers and budgets;
  no libinjection C library is linked into Sibuna. These detectors are used by
  the native CRS transaction engine described in SID 0010.
